---
// The two measured facts a reader can use today, placed right under the hero
// on both front doors (2026-08-20, content-masterclass review). The rule this
// answers: two usable, non-obvious nuggets before the second scroll, and the
// email ask arriving as the answer to the problem the page just raised, not as
// an interruption at the foot.
//
// TRUTH RAILS. Both facts are recorded measurements that already live on the
// tour with their dates and scope; the copy here repeats them, never extends
// them. The probe is dated 2026-07-30 and is Flow's own recorded test of the
// macOS Writing Tools feature; the benchmark figure is one M3 Max on
// 2026-08-18, and "M3 Max" must travel with "4.5 seconds" (the surface test
// asserts it). The score judges speed and fit, never answer quality.
import WaitlistForm from '../ui/WaitlistForm.astro';
import { FLOW_CONSENT_TEXT } from '../../data/flow-consent';

interface Props {
  /** Distinct form id and attribution source per surface. */
  formId: string;
}
const { formId } = Astro.props;
---
<section class="px-6 py-16 sm:py-20" aria-labelledby={`${formId}-heading`}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
      <p class="of-eyebrow" data-animate="rise">Two things we measured</p>
      <h2 id={`${formId}-heading`} class="of-display mt-4 text-[clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem)]" data-animate="lead">A silent rewrite is not a feature. It is a risk.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1fr_0.95fr]" data-animate-stagger="slow">
      <article class="flow-probe of-surface rounded-2xl border border-warn/30 p-6 sm:p-7" data-animate="rise">
        <p class="font-mono text-[0.62rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-accent-ink">Recorded 2026-07-30</p>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-lg font-bold leading-snug">The Mac's own Writing Tools rewrote text inside a code block. Silently.</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
          We tested the system feature on a note that held a code comment with two typos. It
          corrected and capitalized the text inside the code block. No diff shown, no approval
          asked, no record kept. On a real working note, that is corruption of code. We
          reproduced it, dated it, and turned that feature off inside Flow.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-text">What you can use today: check your own notes for code blocks before you let any AI tool loose on them.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="of-surface rounded-2xl border border-border/70 p-6 sm:p-7" data-animate="rise">
        <p class="font-mono text-[0.62rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-accent-ink">Measured 2026-08-18</p>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-lg font-bold leading-snug">The bigger model was more than twice as quick.</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
          On one M3 Max, a 20.4 GB local model answered in 4.5 seconds. An 8.5 GB one took
          10.2. Size did not predict speed; how the model is built did. Flow measures the
          models you already have, on the Mac you are sitting at, and shows the arithmetic.
          The ranking is about speed and fit, never about how good the answers are.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-text">What you can use today: time the first word, not the download size, before you pick a local model.</p>
      </article>
      <div class="of-surface rounded-2xl border border-primary/30 p-6 sm:p-7" data-animate="rise">
        <p class="font-mono text-[0.62rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-primary">If that worries you</p>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-lg font-bold leading-snug">Get the launch note and the receipts as they land.</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
          One email a week at most: what shipped, what was measured, with the dates. Then the
          launch note when Flow is ready.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-5">
          <WaitlistForm
            id={formId}
            source={formId}
            offer="flow-waitlist"
            buttonText="Join the waitlist"
            successMessage="Check your inbox to confirm."
            consentText={FLOW_CONSENT_TEXT}
          />
          <p class="of-waitlist-caption mt-3 font-mono uppercase text-text-dim">
            Free to join · Double opt-in · One email a week, no more
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
